# Milestone Prod-2 Review & Adversarial Challenge Report

**Author**: `reviewer_prod_2_1` (Reviewer & Adversarial Critic)  
**Date**: 2026-11-04T21:53:00Z  
**Target Device**: LG 32LR686BPSA (webOS 8.5.0, Chromium ~108 WAM, SDK 8.5.0, firmware 13.50.44)  
**Verdict**: **APPROVE**  
**Integrity Status**: VERIFIED (No hardcoded facades, shortcuts, or integrity violations)

---

## Review Summary

**Verdict**: APPROVE

Worker `worker_prod_2` has successfully completed all Milestone Prod-2 requirements:
1. `app/js/config.js`: Fixed the priority cascade inversion. `window.PalmSystem.launchParams.proxyUrl` now strictly takes precedence over URL query parameters (`?proxyUrl=`), followed by persistent `localStorage`, and defaulting to `'http://127.0.0.1:8088'`. The explicit override flag (`hasExplicitProxyOverride`) properly protects emergency rollback configurations against dynamic keepalive port mutations.
2. `app/js/app.js`: Auto-spawns the Luna keepalive subscription hook (`luna://com.cinejoy.tv.service/keepalive` with `{ subscribe: true }`) on application initialization supporting native `PalmServiceBridge` and `WebOSServiceBridge` (injected in Chromium WAM) as well as `webOSTV.service.request`. Bridge references are pinned globally to `window._cinejoyLunaBridge` to protect the underlying IPC socket from V8 garbage collection.
3. `app/js/app.js`: Dynamically parses keepalive responses. On valid port assignment, updates `proxyBaseUrl` to `'http://127.0.0.1:<PORT>'` unless an explicit override was supplied. On disconnection or service failure, updates `lunaSubscribed` to `false` and automatically reconnects using exponential backoff clamped safely at 10 seconds.
4. `app/index.html`: Clean script loading order with 100% compatibility with Chromium ~108 and ES5/ES6 webOS runtimes.
5. All 16 automated tests in `tests/test-prod2-keepalive.js` pass with 100% success.
6. All 773 discrete checks across 24 suites in the master regression runner (`npm test`) pass with 100% success (exit code 0).

---

## Integrity & Anti-Cheat Audit

| Check Category | Inspection Focus | Result | Evidence |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Hardcoded Outputs** | Were test assertions or mocks embedded in source files? | **CLEAN** | Source files `app/js/config.js` and `app/js/app.js` contain generic production logic with no hardcoded test conditionals or canned responses. |
| **Facade Implementation** | Is the keepalive or config resolution a non-functional shell? | **CLEAN** | `PalmServiceBridge` and `WebOSServiceBridge` native interfaces, event listeners (`webOSLaunch`, `relaunch`), and JSON parsing logic are genuinely implemented. |
| **Shortcuts & Bypasses** | Did the change bypass required cascade levels? | **CLEAN** | All 4 cascade layers (launchParams > query > localStorage > default) are strictly evaluated in order. |
| **Verification Authenticity** | Were test outputs independently reproduced? | **CLEAN** | Executed both `node tests/test-prod2-keepalive.js` and `npm test` live; verified exit code 0. |

---

## 1. Observation

### 1.1 Priority Cascade in `app/js/config.js`
In `app/js/config.js` lines 120–160:
```javascript
// Base query params
for (var q in urlParams) {
  if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(urlParams, q)) {
    params[q] = urlParams[q];
  }
}

// PalmSystem launch parameters take absolute precedence over URL query parameters
for (var k in palmParams) {
  if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(palmParams, k)) {
    params[k] = palmParams[k];
  }
}

// Exact prioritized cascade in resolving proxyBaseUrl:
// launchParams.proxyUrl > URL query ?proxyUrl= > localStorage.getItem('cinejoy_proxy_url') > default 'http://127.0.0.1:8088'
var resolvedProxyUrl = null;
var hasExplicitOverride = false;
var proxySource = 'default';

if (palmParams && palmParams.proxyUrl) {
  resolvedProxyUrl = palmParams.proxyUrl;
  hasExplicitOverride = true;
  proxySource = 'launchParams';
} else if (urlParams && urlParams.proxyUrl) {
  resolvedProxyUrl = urlParams.proxyUrl;
  hasExplicitOverride = true;
  proxySource = 'query';
} else if (savedProxy) {
  resolvedProxyUrl = savedProxy;
  hasExplicitOverride = false;
  proxySource = 'localStorage';
} else {
  resolvedProxyUrl = 'http://127.0.0.1:8088';
  hasExplicitOverride = false;
  proxySource = 'default';
}

params.proxyUrl = resolvedProxyUrl;
CINEJOY_CONFIG.proxyBaseUrl = resolvedProxyUrl;
CINEJOY_CONFIG.hasExplicitProxyOverride = hasExplicitOverride;
CINEJOY_CONFIG.proxySource = proxySource;
```
Direct observation: `palmParams.proxyUrl` is checked first. If present, `hasExplicitOverride` is set to `true` and `proxySource` is set to `'launchParams'`. URL query parameters (`urlParams.proxyUrl`) only apply if `palmParams.proxyUrl` is absent, and `localStorage` only applies if both are absent. Default `'http://127.0.0.1:8088'` applies when all three are absent. The previous priority inversion where query parameters blindly overwrote `palmParams` has been fully eliminated.

### 1.2 Native Luna Keepalive Hook in `app/js/app.js`
In `app/js/app.js` lines 120–204:
```javascript
var Bridge = (typeof window !== 'undefined' && (window.PalmServiceBridge || window.WebOSServiceBridge)) || null;
if (Bridge) {
  try {
    console.log('[CinejoyApp] Registering Luna keepalive via native PalmServiceBridge / WebOSServiceBridge...');
    var bridge = new Bridge();
    bridge.onservicecallback = function (msg) {
      try {
        var res = typeof msg === 'string' ? JSON.parse(msg) : msg;
        if (res && res.returnValue !== false) {
          self.handleKeepaliveSuccess(res);
        } else {
          self.handleKeepaliveFailure(res);
        }
      } catch (e) {
        console.warn('[CinejoyApp] Native bridge payload parse error:', e);
        self.handleKeepaliveFailure(e);
      }
    };

    bridge.call(serviceUri + '/' + method, JSON.stringify({ subscribe: true }));

    // Store on window and app state to prevent garbage collection of IPC socket
    if (typeof window !== 'undefined') {
      window._cinejoyLunaBridge = bridge;
    }
    this.state.lunaBridge = bridge;
    return bridge;
  } catch (err) { ... }
}
```
Direct observation: The hook checks `window.PalmServiceBridge || window.WebOSServiceBridge` (as well as `webOSTV.service.request`), issues a subscription request `{ subscribe: true }` to `luna://com.cinejoy.tv.service/keepalive`, and assigns the bridge instance to `window._cinejoyLunaBridge` and `this.state.lunaBridge` to prevent V8 garbage collection of the underlying native bridge object.

### 1.3 Dynamic Port Resolution & Override Protection
In `app/js/app.js` lines 216–259:
```javascript
handleKeepaliveSuccess: function (res) {
  this.state.lunaSubscribed = true;
  this.state.lunaUptime = res && res.uptime;
  ...
  if (res && typeof res.port === 'number' && res.port > 0) {
    var port = res.port;
    this.state.activeProxyPort = port;

    var hasExplicitOverride = false;
    if (typeof window !== 'undefined' && window.CINEJOY_CONFIG) {
      hasExplicitOverride = !!window.CINEJOY_CONFIG.hasExplicitProxyOverride;
    }

    if (!hasExplicitOverride) {
      var newProxyUrl = 'http://127.0.0.1:' + port;
      if (typeof window !== 'undefined') {
        if (window.CINEJOY_CONFIG) {
          window.CINEJOY_CONFIG.proxyBaseUrl = newProxyUrl;
          if (typeof window.CINEJOY_CONFIG.setProxyUrl === 'function') {
            window.CINEJOY_CONFIG.setProxyUrl(newProxyUrl);
          }
        }
        if (window.PlayerController) {
          window.PlayerController._customProxyBaseUrl = newProxyUrl;
        }
      }
      if (typeof global !== 'undefined' && global.CINEJOY_CONFIG) {
        global.CINEJOY_CONFIG.proxyBaseUrl = newProxyUrl;
      }
      console.log('[CinejoyApp] Dynamic proxy port updated to: ' + port + ' (' + newProxyUrl + ')');
    } else {
      console.log('[CinejoyApp] Explicit proxy override active; preserving override: ' + (window.CINEJOY_CONFIG && window.CINEJOY_CONFIG.proxyBaseUrl));
    }
  }
}
```
Direct observation: Dynamic port updating verifies that `res.port` is a valid positive number. It consults `window.CINEJOY_CONFIG.hasExplicitProxyOverride`. If an explicit override exists (`launchParams` or query string), the override is preserved and port mutation is skipped. If default or localStorage was used, `proxyBaseUrl` and `PlayerController._customProxyBaseUrl` are updated synchronously to `'http://127.0.0.1:' + port`.

### 1.4 Auto-Reconnection & Backoff Clamping
In `app/js/app.js` lines 265–285:
```javascript
handleKeepaliveFailure: function (err) {
  this.state.lunaSubscribed = false;
  console.warn('[CinejoyApp] Luna keepalive subscription failed or disconnected:', err);

  var self = this;
  if (!this._lunaReconnectDelay) {
    this._lunaReconnectDelay = 1000;
  }

  if (this._lunaReconnectTimer) {
    clearTimeout(this._lunaReconnectTimer);
  }

  this._lunaReconnectTimer = setTimeout(function () {
    self._lunaReconnectTimer = null;
    self._lunaReconnectDelay = Math.min(self._lunaReconnectDelay * 1.5, 10000);
    console.log('[CinejoyApp] Attempting Luna keepalive reconnection...');
    self.initLunaKeepalive();
  }, this._lunaReconnectDelay);
}
```
Direct observation: Any pending timer is cleared before setting a new one. Backoff starts at 1,000ms, multiplies by 1.5 per retry, and clamps at 10,000ms (10 seconds) via `Math.min(..., 10000)`.

### 1.5 HTML Script Order
In `app/index.html` lines 1243–1253:
```html
